# Testing Conventions

## Framework

- Vitest with `jsdom` environment (configured in `vitest.config.ts`)
- Globals enabled: `describe`, `it`, `expect`, `vi` available without imports
- Path alias: `@` resolves to `src/`

## Test Organization

- Unit tests: `src/__tests__/unit/<ModuleName>.test.ts` — mirrors source file names
- Integration tests: `src/__tests__/integration/`
- Mocks: `src/__tests__/mocks/jssip.ts` (JsSIP UA mock), `src/__tests__/mocks/fixtures.ts`
- Setup: `src/__tests__/setup.ts`

## Running Tests

- `npm run test:run` for single CI run
- `npm run test` for watch mode during development
- `npm run test:coverage` to check 80% threshold compliance

## Writing Tests

- Mock JsSIP using the existing mock in `src/__tests__/mocks/jssip.ts`
- Use fixtures from `src/__tests__/mocks/fixtures.ts` for test data
- Test both success paths and error/edge cases
- Avoid real network calls — mock `fetch` and WebSocket
